          {
            "say": "Here is the pseudocode for standard bubble sort. The outer loop runs $n$ times, and the inner loop compares adjacent elements up to $n$ minus $i$ minus $1$, shrinking as the largest elements settle at the end.",
            "draw": [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "for i from 0 to n-1:",
                "tone": "normal"
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "for j from 0 to n-i-2:",
                "tone": "normal"
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "if A[j] > A[j+1] swap(A[j], A[j+1])",
                "tone": "important"
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "say": "To find the worst case time complexity, we count the total number of comparisons. On pass one, we do $n-1$ comparisons, then $n-2$, all the way down to just $1$ comparison on the final pass.",
            "draw": [
              {
                "type": "math",
                "latex": "T(n) = \\sum_{i=1}^{n-1} (n - i)",
                "label": "Total comparisons",
                "boxed": true
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "say": "Let's expand this summation. It is equal to $(n-1)$ plus $(n-2)$ plus all the way down to $1$. Using our arithmetic series sum formula, this evaluates to $n$ times $n-1$ over $2$.",
            "draw": [
              {
                "type": "steps",
                "lines": [
